## Sparse voxel grids, NanoVDB-like (design D9): a flat, read-only layout of
## 8×8×8 leaves, published once and shared by count. A grid is its leaves'
## sorted keys (Morton codes of leaf coordinates), 512 f32 values a leaf (x
## fastest, then y, then z) and 8 active-mask words a leaf, an index-to-world
## affine transform and a background value for everything outside the
## leaves. Builders fill leaves in parallel and publish a new grid; nothing
## writes a published one.
##
## A level set (class level_set) stores signed distances in a narrow band
## around the surface, negative inside; a fog volume (class fog) stores
## densities. Voxel (i, j, k) sits at transform (i, j, k).
